# wakir-persona-engine — runtime image for the Wakir persona-engine
# pilot binary (Sprint-10 Tag-4, ADR-0058 Pilot-Phase Schritt 9).
#
# Substrate scope (0.1.0-pilot)
# -----------------------------
# This is the **substrate-closer** image for ADR-0058 Schritt 9. The
# Quadlet ``quadlet/wakir-persona-tomas.container`` (Selin Sprint-
# Pengine-7 Tag-5 OI-PILOT-1) was authored against
# ``ghcr.io/wakir-labs/wakir-persona-engine:0.1.0-pilot`` ahead of the
# binary itself landing; this image fills the substrate gap so the
# Pilot-VM can launch the Tomás-Doppelbetrieb-Shadow without further
# image-availability blockers.
#
# The 0.1.0-pilot binary is a deliberately minimal Python stub
# exposing the persona-engine CLI surface declared in
# ``wirelang/specs/persona-engine-format-spec.md`` §"CLI invocation
# contract" (``spawn`` + ``healthcheck`` subcommands) with the
# Env-var contract declared in §"Env var contract". The full Rust
# implementation lands on the Sprint-Pengine-8 axis (Selin); when
# that lands, this image's tag rotates to ``0.2.0-pilot`` (or
# ``1.0.0``) and the same Quadlet pin-rotation workflow
# (``resolve-image-pins-ci``) closes the swap idempotently.
#
# Why ship the stub
# -----------------
# Three options were on the table (Tomás Sprint-10 Tag-4 substrate-
# gap-analysis 2026-05-15):
#
#   A) Block ADR-0058 Schritt 9 until Sprint-Pengine-8 lands the full
#      persona-engine. Cost: Pilot-Phase opens delayed; Doppelbetrieb
#      4-Wochen-Clock starts later than approved.
#   B) Hand-roll a podman-run command outside the Quadlet substrate
#      until the engine lands. Cost: bypasses the audit substrate
#      (Quadlet healthcheck, restart policy, named-volume lifecycle);
#      the Doppelbetrieb-Vergleich runs on a non-substrate spawn.
#   C) Ship a substrate-stub image now that satisfies the Quadlet
#      contract (CLI surface, healthcheck, Env-var contract,
#      Sigstore-keyless-signed digest) and rotate to the real engine
#      when Sprint-Pengine-8 lands. Cost: the Doppelbetrieb-Vergleich
#      4-Wochen-Clock starts on a stub-engine that emits stub-output
#      and does not yet drive comparable Engineering traffic.
#
# Mira-Hand-Decision 2026-05-15: option C, because the substrate-
# layer (Quadlet, SPIRE-SVID, NATS-KV bucket, Doppelbetrieb-Shadow
# bridging) is the actual ADR-0058 Schritt 9 risk-surface — those
# moving pieces benefit from running against a real Pilot-VM with a
# stub engine, not from waiting until the engine is real to find out
# whether the substrate is sound. The 4-Wochen-Clock is qualified:
# stub-period output is excluded from the 4-Achsen-Score-Bilanz; the
# clock effectively starts when 0.2.0 lands. See ADR-0058 §"Pilot-
# Phase Substrate-Gap-Closer".
#
# Image scope (v0.1.0-pilot, substrate-stub)
# ------------------------------------------
# The image carries exactly the runtime wheel set:
#
#   * (none) — the stub is pure CPython stdlib (json, os, sys,
#     signal, time, hashlib). The Sprint-Pengine-8 successor image
#     will pull in nats-py + cryptography for SVID-fetch + NATS-KV
#     state-pack persistence; the stub does neither (it emits the
#     stub-mode telemetry log line and idles on SIGTERM).
#
# The image deliberately does NOT carry the wakir-runtime tree
# itself. The runtime is bind-mounted into the container from the
# host at ``/opt/wakir-runtime`` (see Quadlet ``Volume=`` lines);
# the persona-engine binary itself ships in the image at
# ``/opt/wakir/bin/persona-engine``.
#
# BSL-1.1 + image provenance
# --------------------------
# The image as a whole is published under the Business Source
# License 1.1 (parity with the wakir-provisioner image,
# AR-Decision 2026-05-13, consistent with the WAT-Pipeline-Server
# Phase-1a BSL pattern per ADR-0034). CPython stdlib ships under
# PSF-2.0 and is reachable via ``python3 --version`` inside the
# container; the BSL header on the image as a whole does not extend
# to the stdlib. The BSL Additional Use Grant permits self-hosting
# for own-org operations; commercial multi-tenant hosting requires a
# separate Wakir-Cloud licence. The image automatically converts to
# Apache-2.0 four years after the first BSL-licensed image
# publication (Change Date: 2030-05-15).
#
# Build path: ``.github/workflows/build-wakir-persona-engine.yml``
# (Operator-Hand ``workflow_dispatch`` only; pushes to
# ``ghcr.io/wakir-labs/wakir-persona-engine:<tag>``).
#
# Pin path: ``scripts/image-pin-idempotent-resolver.sh`` PINS array
# carries the ``wakir_persona_engine`` row; the Quadlet
# ``quadlet/wakir-persona-tomas.container`` references the digest-
# pinned form ``ghcr.io/wakir-labs/wakir-persona-engine:0.1.0-pilot
# @sha256:<digest>``.

FROM docker.io/library/python:3.13-slim@sha256:DIGEST_PENDING_TOMAS_REVIEW

# OCI metadata. The build workflow stamps build-time labels
# (``org.opencontainers.image.revision`` etc.) at push time.
LABEL org.opencontainers.image.title="wakir-persona-engine"
LABEL org.opencontainers.image.description="Runtime image for the Wakir persona-engine pilot binary (Sprint-10 Tag-4, v0.1.0-pilot substrate-stub closing the ADR-0058 Schritt 9 image-availability gap; full engine lands on the Sprint-Pengine-8 axis)."
LABEL org.opencontainers.image.version="0.1.0-pilot"
LABEL org.opencontainers.image.licenses="BUSL-1.1"
LABEL org.opencontainers.image.source="https://github.com/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime"
LABEL org.opencontainers.image.url="https://github.com/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime"
LABEL org.opencontainers.image.documentation="https://github.com/wakir-labs/wakir-runtime/blob/main/infra/persona-engine/README.md"

# Non-root runtime user, matching the Quadlet ``User=1000`` /
# ``Group=1000``. We do not chown ``/opt/wakir-runtime`` because the
# runtime bind-mount supplies its own ownership semantics at unit
# start. We DO chown the ``/opt/wakir/bin`` directory so the
# persona-engine binary is executable as uid 1000 from the
# read-only-root filesystem of the Quadlet.
RUN groupadd --gid 1000 wakir \
    && useradd --uid 1000 --gid 1000 --no-create-home --shell /usr/sbin/nologin wakir \
    && mkdir -p /opt/wakir/bin \
    && chown -R 1000:1000 /opt/wakir

# Ship the persona-engine stub binary. The script is pure CPython
# stdlib; no pip step needed.
COPY --chown=1000:1000 bin/persona-engine /opt/wakir/bin/persona-engine
RUN chmod 0755 /opt/wakir/bin/persona-engine

USER 1000:1000
WORKDIR /opt/wakir-runtime

# Make the entrypoint discoverable for callers that invoke the image
# directly (debugging, smoke). The Quadlet supplies its own
# ``Exec=spawn --persona-slug tomas --pilot-phase doppelbetrieb-shadow``
# line; this ENTRYPOINT ensures that line resolves to the persona-
# engine binary even when the Quadlet's command-line parsing is the
# only contract the runtime sees.
ENTRYPOINT ["/opt/wakir/bin/persona-engine"]
